captain francis pike leads his team  across the arctic tundra in the distance  they can see the city of  autopapadopoulos  it flows 7.8 kilometers above the ground  and is filled with mysteries and  treasures beyond even the foundation's  wildest dreams  it is september of 1933 when the scp  foundation first catches winds of  something odd going on in the arctic a  british airman named sir george danson  flies over the north sea heading to  norway after he lands in oslo danson  begins ranting about a floating city the  foundation immediately disseminates  contradictory information and  manipulates the story to include that  danson had been drinking during his  flight so everything he is saying is  probably the result of a drunken  hallucination while scp agents spread  lies the foundation immediately launches  an investigation the team that is sent  to the arctic confirms what danson  claims to have seen there is indeed a  floating city there now captain pike and  his team stare at the island in the sky  as their hot air balloons are filled  behind them the arctic wind whips up  small snow tornadoes as the temperature  plummets the balloons are ready and pike  orders his men to board they lift off  from the ground and pull their parka  hoods over their heads to protect them  from the arctic blasts at high altitudes  pike and his team slowly drift over the  city of autopapadopoulos when they are  somewhat in the middle of the floating  island the hot air balloons are lowered  and the team lands without incident to  their surprise the exploratory team  finds that the floating city has its own  microclimate which is much more pleasant  than the frigid arctic they remove their  winter gear proceed with caution pike  tells his men we have no idea what we're  going to find in the city the  architecture is clearly old but not  exactly like anything on earth today it  seems to be a conglomerate of ancient  mesopotamian design mixed with the  design features of several other  cultures many of the buildings that line  the stone streets are crumbling and the  city overall is in ruins pike leads his  team down a series of roads scientists  photograph and take notes of the city  for foundation records scp agents check  around every corner to make sure there  is nothing hiding in the shadows the  team comes to a crossroads halt bike  shouts standing in front of them is an  old man with long gray hair and a white  beard he seems to be of middle eastern  descent hello friends the old man says  welcome to ariba padopoulos i am the  caretaker of the city i've been  expecting you please follow me the old  man turns around and proceeds down the  causeway pike hesitates for a moment  stay alert he whispers to the agents  behind him then he begins to follow the  old man down the street as pike walks he  takes in the grandeur that the city once  held the roads are as wide as the main  avenues back in london while the  buildings although in shambles still  retains some of their ancient beauty  pike begins to walk a little faster to  catch up with the old man what happened  here he asks the man turns his head all  will be revealed soon francis pike just  be patient how do you know my name asks  spike the old man smiles they turn  another corner and in front of them is  the grand hall it seems to have survived  whatever catastrophe befell the rest of  the city pike stops and stares up at the  massive structure with his mouth ajar  come says the old man as he motions the  scp team to follow him up the steps into  the main hall let's eat the old man  prepares a simple meal but one that  fills the stomachs and satisfies pyke  and his men at the conclusion of the  meal captain pike approaches the  mysterious man i feel like you deserve  an explanation as to who we are and why  we're here pike says the old man raises  his hand you are from the foundation he  replies i already know about the  foundation and you french's pike i have  been waiting for you to arrive for a  long time there are things i need to  show you in the city there are old  secrets and ancient relics from the past  that you were sent here to learn about  pike looks at the men in squints what  are you talking about how could you know  we were coming and what relics are you  referring to exactly the old man grins  and places a hand on captain pike's  shoulder pike feels a longing emotion  well up inside of him it's as if he has  been waiting for this moment his whole  life come says the old man you and your  man need rest he shows pike and the  exploration team to several rooms down  the hallway where they can set up for  the night the rooms are large and  comfortable sleep well french's pike  tomorrow i have much to show you the old  man leaves the room and proceeds down  the hallway to his small humble chamber  the next morning pike and the other scp  agents are greeted by the rising sun and  the old man waiting for them on the  steps of the grand hall he leads them  through the city there are three temples  i wish to show you the old man says to  pike you will notice that their  architecture and imagery differ from  most of the other structures in the city  make sure you listen very carefully  frances pike as what you're about to  learn could save the universe or perhaps  destroy it pike is speechless all he can  do is nod his head the old man leads the  scp agents to the middle of the city  where the three temples reside each one  has its own unique iconography and style  the art seems to reflect important  events in history or subjects that hold  significance in the past the old man  proceeds to walk towards the first  temple upon entering the structure there  is a mural of two naked people watching  the horizon from a tree line behind them  are a wolf and bear that seem to be  protectively standing guard directly  opposite of this picture is a painting  of a figure holding a flaming sword on a  hill as pike and his team enter the main  hall they 