m a pair of thermal imaging  goggles pike puts them on damn pike  mutters with the thermal lenses on he  can now see a massive humanoid entity  lying dead on the floor his body is so  large that it covers the murals on three  of the walls pike notices that the  temperature in the room is still  continuing to increase as the dead giant  is radiating heat the foundation  classifies the entity as  scp-4840-b it has six arms and six legs  each connected by metal chains to iron  flails at the end a sigil has been  brandished into the middle of the  entity's chest what is that pike asks  the old man just shakes his head one of  the many who have fallen he responds the  old man points to the only wall that is  not blocked by the massive body of  scp-4840-b and frowns the golden man is  depicted here as well pai can't help but  feel there is some sort of connection  between adudpadopoulos the old man and  the golden figure he keeps seeing in the  murals in the temple of sunset the  golden man sits atop a white horse with  his iron crown resting on his head  behind him is a massive army of men and  women holding axes and swords across  from the golden man and his army are  legions of green and gray figures with  six eyes dressed in brilliantly colored  clothing an intense lightning storm  appears to be amassing in the distance  captain pike looks up to the ceiling to  see it covered in stars however he does  not recognize any of the constellations  is the golden man i keep seeing but  before pike can finish his question the  old man cuts him off we must be going he  turns and exits the temple bike does not  want to push the old man he seems to be  a wealth of knowledge and the only way  to learn more about autodapadopoulos and  what it all means they exit the temple  of sunset and continue to the final  structure in the middle of the city the  old man leads pike and the rest of the  scp agents to the smallest temple of the  three he stops just outside of the  doorway this is the temple of the night  he proclaims what you see on the surface  is deceiving this temple goes deep  underground it contains a labyrinth of  passages that one could get lost in  forever so please be careful are you  coming pike asks no response the old man  i do not enter the temple of night i  have my reasons which do not concern you  pike nods and then signals his men to  follow him into the temple he notices  that many of the murals in the  passageways and rooms of the temple of  night depict the same image of a massive  tree in the middle of a vast forest in  each instance of the tree there seemed  to be red lights surrounding the base  human-like figures hanging from its  branches and structures wrapped in vines  surrounding the trunk the hallways are  illuminated by some unknown light source  it is as if torches line the walls and  give off a dull yellowish glow but there  is no fire to be seen  embedded in the walls are sarcophagi  with intricate carvings in their stone  casings pike can't help but notice  scratching sounds coming from within the  sarcophagi as if someone or something is  trying to claw its way out the  exploration team reaches the innermost  chamber of the temple there is a  staircase in the middle of the room that  descends below the floor however its  entrance is covered by rubble from a  collapsed wall suddenly an scp agent  runs up to captain pike sir i think you  should see this pike follows the man  back through a series of twists and  turns he stops at a closed door the  foundation's seal is carved into the  wood it seems as if the carving has been  there for a long time which is  impossible since they are the first scp  team to explore the city of  otadapadopoulos the agent pushes open  the door and pike steps in he is  astonished by what he finds it seems he  has been transported to an abandoned  foundation site all of the lights are  off but he can tell that it is some kind  of central command center due to the  screens and setup of the space painted  in black block letters on one of the  walls is site site000  pike quickly exits back through the  entryway and shuts the door behind him  he looks at the scp agent who brought  him into the room secure the store and  make sure no one gets in or comes out do  i make myself clear pike orders his men  to exit the temple after everyone comes  out captain pike walks over to the old  man who is sitting on the steps outside  did you find what you are looking for  francis pike the old man asks captain  pike shakes his head he stares down eyes  wide at the stone steps of the temple as  she says the old man i have something  else to show you francis pike the old  man leads pike to the grand hall that  they had slept in the night before he  brings him through a series of  passageways and down a staircase they  stop in front of a large door open it  the old man whispers captain francis  pike walks up to the door and pushes it  open on the other side is endless  darkness from which he hears his own  voice speaking to him through the ether  pike begins to walk towards the darkness  the old man places his hand on pike's  shoulder and pulls him back then he  shuts the door the light of the world  has long since left that place and  mortal men can no longer walk it says  the old man i needed to show it to you  as a warning things are not always what  they seem francis pike that night pike  lies awake staring at the ceiling of the  grand hall thinking about the old man  he sits up and begins jotting down his  thoughts in his official report he  identifies the old man as  scp-4840-a but in his journal he can't  help but refer to him as a friend there  is something about the old man  something special pike knows there is  much more to his story and the story of  the flying city of ottada padopoulos now  watch  scp-001 or a borrow cycle the full story  compilation scp animation or check out  scp-5000 why the full story compilation  scp animation

